sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: A first bimedial straight line is divided at one and the same point only.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be a first bimedial straight line divided at {C}, so that {AC} and {CB} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a rational rectangle. [!just X.37]

I say that {AB} is not so divided at another point.

If possible, let it also be divided at {D}, so that {AD} and {DB} are also medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a rational rectangle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="270" height="70" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.43 diagram" src="propX43.gif"/></noscript>
